---
source: crates/runtime/src/builder.rs
expression: "[refused(decide(&[(CAYENNE_DISK_CACHE_MB_PARAM, \"lots\"),\n(CAYENNE_VNEXT_PARAM, \"enabled\")], Some(&s3), None,)),\nrefused(decide(&[(CAYENNE_DISK_CACHE_MB_PARAM, \"512\")], Some(&s3), None)),\nrefused(decide(&on, Some(&s3), Some(&ClusterRole::Executor))),\nrefused(decide(&on, None, None)),\nrefused(decide(&on, Some(&state(\"file:///srv/state/\")), None)),\nrefused(decide(&on, Some(&state(\"gs://bucket/state/\")), None)),].join(\"\\n\")"
---
The Cayenne disk cache is off: `runtime.params.cayenne_disk_cache_mb` is 'lots', not a number of MiB, so every read of Cayenne data goes to the object store. Set it to the most MiB the cache may use, or to 0 to turn the cache off. See: https://spiceai.org/docs/components/data-accelerators/cayenne
The Cayenne disk cache is off: `runtime.params.cayenne_disk_cache_mb` is set, but the cache serves only data Cayenne keeps in `runtime.state.location`, which needs `runtime.params.cayenne_vnext: enabled`, so every read of Cayenne data goes to its local files. Enable `cayenne_vnext`, or remove `cayenne_disk_cache_mb`. See: https://spiceai.org/docs/components/data-accelerators/cayenne
The Cayenne disk cache is off: `runtime.params.cayenne_disk_cache_mb` is set, but a cluster scheduler or executor keeps its Cayenne data on local disk, so there is nothing for the cache to serve. Remove `cayenne_disk_cache_mb`. See: https://spiceai.org/docs/components/data-accelerators/cayenne
The Cayenne disk cache is off: `runtime.params.cayenne_disk_cache_mb` is set, but `runtime.state.location` is not, so Cayenne keeps its data on local disk and there is nothing for the cache to serve. Set `runtime.state.location` to an `s3://` location, or remove `cayenne_disk_cache_mb`. See: https://spiceai.org/docs/components/data-accelerators/cayenne
The Cayenne disk cache is off: `runtime.params.cayenne_disk_cache_mb` is set, but `runtime.state.location` 'file:///srv/state/' is not an `s3://` location, and the cache serves only data in S3. Move `runtime.state.location` to S3, or remove `cayenne_disk_cache_mb`. See: https://spiceai.org/docs/components/data-accelerators/cayenne
The Cayenne disk cache is off: `runtime.params.cayenne_disk_cache_mb` is set, but `runtime.state.location` 'gs://bucket/state/' is not an `s3://` location, and the cache serves only data in S3. Move `runtime.state.location` to S3, or remove `cayenne_disk_cache_mb`. See: https://spiceai.org/docs/components/data-accelerators/cayenne
